Implement user story SKY-002-b: Test SkyscannerClient with mocked fetch and mock-mode verification

## Story Description
Create src/skyscanner/client.test.ts with vitest tests that mock global fetch (no real network calls). Covers: URL/header construction, successful response parsing, HTTP error rejection, missing-key constructor errors, malformed response handling, and mock-mode behavior verification.

## Acceptance Criteria
- client.test.ts uses vitest with mocked global fetch (vi.stubGlobal or equivalent) and afterEach restoration; no real network calls
- Test verifies correct RapidAPI URL and header construction (including X-RapidAPI-Key header with the resolved apiKey)
- Test verifies successful API response is parsed into FlightResult[] with correct field mapping
- Test verifies HTTP 4xx/5xx response causes searchFlights to reject with Error including status code in message
- Test verifies missing or empty apiKey (both constructor arg and RAPIDAPI_KEY env var) throws missing-key Error
- Test verifies malformed or missing-fields response body causes searchFlights to reject with parse/validation Error
- Test verifies MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API='true' returns fixture without invoking fetch (spy/assert never called); non-'true' values (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') perform real fetch call
- tsc --noEmit and vitest run both exit 0 with all tests passing


## Test Criteria (ground truth — written from actual source; overrides any conflicting AC)
- SkyscannerClient class exported from './skyscanner/client'
- Constructor signature: constructor({ apiKey }: { apiKey?: string } = {})
- Constructor throws Error with exact message: 'SkyscannerClient requires an apiKey. Provide it via constructor or set RAPIDAPI_KEY environment variable.' when apiKey is undefined, null, empty string, or whitespace-only string
- Constructor reads apiKey from constructor arg first, falls back to process.env.RAPIDAPI_KEY
- searchFlights method signature: async searchFlights(params: SearchParams): Promise<FlightResult[]>
- SearchParams interface: { origin: string; destination: string; date: string; adults?: number }
- FlightResult interface: { price: number; currency: string; airline: string; departure: string; arrival: string; duration: number; stops: number }
- MOCK_SKYSCANNER_API env check: exact string 'true' triggers mock mode, all other values (unset, empty, 'false', '1', 'TRUE') perform real fetch
- Mock mode returns hardcoded array of 3 FlightResult objects from getMockFlightResults() without calling fetch
- Real API URL: https://skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com/flights/search with query params origin, destination, date, adults
- Query param adults defaults to 1 if not provided
- Headers sent: 'X-RapidAPI-Key' with this.#apiKey, 'X-RapidAPI-Host': 'skyscanner44.p.rapidapi.com'
- HTTP error handling: throws Error with message 'HTTP error: ${response.status} ${response.statusText}' for non-ok responses
- Response parsing: checks data is object, extracts results from data.results || data.flights || data
- Response validation: throws Error 'Invalid response: expected JSON object' if data not object
- Response validation: throws Error 'Invalid response: expected results array' if results not array
- Each flight result validated by isValidFlightResult: requires price (number), currency (string), airline (string), departure (string), arrival (string), duration (number), stops (number)
- Validation error: throws Error 'Invalid flight result: missing or invalid required fields' for invalid items
- No validation for adults parameter (can be 0, negative, or any number)
- No validation for origin/destination/date format or content

## Mock Strategy
```typescript
vi.mock('<import-path-to-SkyscannerClient>', () => ({
  SkyscannerClient: vi.fn().mockImplementation(() => ({
    searchFlights: vi.fn().mockResolvedValue(undefined),
    isValidFlightResult: vi.fn(),
    getMockFlightResults: vi.fn(),
  })),
}));
```

